**Thread 6 (fold remainder formatting)** — RED first. Add a test in the comment-composition suite. Let me add after the AC2 test or at suite end. I'll add a new test:

```js
test('review follow-up (gh-1063 thread 6): the fold remainder lines use the same bullet+<code> format as the 3 previews', function() {
   var threads = [];
   for (var i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
       threads.push(ghThread('PRT_' + i, i, { body: 'Finding number ' + i + ' needs a fix' }));
   }
   var c = commentFor(threads, [], 'reason text', null);
   var afterMore = c.substring(c.indexOf('…and'));
   assert.equal(afterMore.split('- <code>').length - 1, 2,
       'the 2 remainder lines carry the same "- <code>…</code>" format as the 3 previews');
   assert.notContains(afterMore.split('…and 2 more:')[1], '\nPRT_',
       'no plain-text remainder line inside the fold');
});
```

Hmm the notContains check: remainder lines previously were plain `PRT_4 — ... With fix they're `- <code>PRT_4 — ... So `afterMore` should not contain a line starting with 'PRT_'. Simpler assertion: count occurrences. Let me use: assert that every line containing 'PRT_4' starts with '- <code>'. Keep it simple:

```js
var foldLines = c.split('\n').filter(function(l) { return l.indexOf('PRT_4') !== -1; });
assert.equal(foldLines.length, 1);
assert.equal(foldLines[0].indexOf('- <code>'), 0, 'remainder line is buleted + code-formatted');
```

