arguments.content:
Fixed — the fold remainder now renders uniformly. In `buildUnaddressedThreadsFold` (`js/pushReworkChanges.js`) the lines after "…and N more:" are wrapped exactly like the 3 previews:

```js
unaddressed.slice(3).forEach(function(t) {
    lines.push('- <code>' + threadShortLabel(t, 20) + '</code>');
});
```

One deliberate deviation from the literal suggestion: the label cap drops `32 → 20`, because the wrapper adds 14 chars per line and at 32 the 39-thread AC2 case blew the ~2000-char comment budget (measured 2379). At 20 the full list stays uniform **and** the 39-thread comment is back under 2000 chars.

Regression test (RED-verified against the pre-fix head): `review follow-up (gh-1063 thread 6)` in the comment-composition suite — 5-thread case asserting both remainder lines are bulleted `<code>` items. Suite: 134 passed, 0 failed.

